An article is sold for ₹1,440 at a profit of 20%. What was its cost price?

A) ₹1,100
B) ₹1,200
C) ₹1,250
D) ₹1,300

Answer: B) ₹1,200

Explanation:

A 20% profit means:

$$ SP=120\%\text{ of CP} $$

So:

$$ 1440=\frac{120}{100}\times CP $$

Therefore:

$$ CP=1440\times\frac{100}{120} $$ $$ =\boxed{₹1,200} $$

✅ Answer: B) ₹1,200
